            <ArticleTitle>Values and problems in MR imaging for the evaluation of low back pain (orthopedic surgeon's view).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>127-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>MR imaging has a significant diagnostic value, but abnormal findings revealed by MR imaging do not always cause symptoms. MR imaging findings should be confirmed by subjective symptoms, objective findings, and functional diagnostic procedures.</AbstractText>
